# Fork-only override of the root .gitignore's `docs/superpowers/*` rule, which
# arrived from upstream in 4d5d9fffd0 (PR #56582). Upstream ignores this path;
# this fork deliberately TRACKS what lives here -- specs, plans, audits,
# canaries, and rollout evidence are durable design artifacts, not scratch.
#
# Why here and not next to the rule in the root .gitignore: upstream edits that
# file on nearly every release merge, so a fork-only negation there is a
# recurring conflict point. Patterns in a subdirectory's .gitignore override
# those from parent directories, and this file un-ignores itself below, so the
# root file stays byte-identical to upstream.
#
# What this fixes: without it, every new spec or plan needed `git add -f`, which
# cannot be done through the mandatory git-quiet-commit.py wrapper (it has no
# force-add flag). The workaround was a bare `git add -f` followed by
# `git-quiet-commit.py --index-as-is`, leaving a staged file in the SHARED index
# between the two calls. On 2026-08-13 that window was hit and a 365-line spec
# was swept into a concurrent session's unrelated commit (93486b7d16).
#
# New subdirectories stay ignored by default. Add a negation below when a subdir
# holds durable artifacts; leave it out when it holds scratch or build output.
!.gitignore
!specs/
!plans/
!audits/
!canaries/
!rollout-evidence/
